(457901, 42227, 4543, '<td valign="top">You are the master!  Congrats again, perfect execution!</td>', 'You are the master!  Congrats again, perfect execution!', '2003-10-22 09:55:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(457905, 41756, 12855, '<td valign="top">Wow, I wasn''t expecting so much negative feedback. Granted the picture is grainy, but when I lightened it up so people could see the figures better, I couldn''t avoid the effect. If you can''t make it out, it''s a white girl with a black man standing behind her. I took the picture of the reflection of the two in a window. It was dark out and the orange blur next to the girl is a street light from a city that lies about a mile away. I thought it would be different for a change. I guess it was too different. Not many people could understand what it was. Maybe a better title next time? Someone said it was blurry and mentioned the use of a tripod...might work...but the blury effect is from the window, sort of like the effect water has on a reflection...it''s called science. It isn''t perfect and it''s hardly ever an exact. It''s called an experiment with film and reflections...guess the experiment was a bomb...</td>', 'Wow, I wasn''t expecting so much negative feedback. Granted the picture is grainy, but when I lightened it up so people could see the figures better, I couldn''t avoid the effect. If you can''t make it out, it''s a white girl with a black man standing behind her. I took the picture of the reflection of the two in a window. It was dark out and the orange blur next to the girl is a street light from a city that lies about a mile away. I thought it would be different for a change. I guess it was too different. Not many people could understand what it was. Maybe a better title next time? Someone said it was blurry and mentioned the use of a tripod...might work...but the blury effect is from the window, sort of like the effect water has on a reflection...it''s called science. It isn''t perfect and it''s hardly ever an exact. It''s called an experiment with film and reflections...guess the experiment was a bomb...', '2003-10-22 10:00:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(457911, 42227, 10985, '<td valign="top">Eeeexcellent! So graphically appealing. The fact that the drops are of gradually increasing or decreasing sizes adds a lot to that. A beauty!</td>', 'Eeeexcellent! So graphically appealing. The fact that the drops are of gradually increasing or decreasing sizes adds a lot to that. A beauty!', '2003-10-22 10:03:10.000000', NULL, 0),
