(458119, 42227, 9452, '<td valign="top">I don´t know what to say, i´ll been follow your work, and i think you''re amazing good, if you´re not a profesional photographer, man, you''re wasting your time.<br/>"A brilliant mind is not the one that make extraordinary things, but the one that make from the ordinary something extraordinary"</td>', 'I don´t know what to say, i´ll been follow your work, and i think you''re amazing good, if you´re not a profesional photographer, man, you''re wasting your time."A brilliant mind is not the one that make extraordinary things, but the one that make from the ordinary something extraordinary"', '2003-10-22 12:07:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(458147, 42225, 11687, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dave Gordon:</b></div><hr/><i>Are the colors this brilliant to the naked eye, or do they depend on a photgraphic medium to bring them out?</i></td></tr></table> <br/>They are this brilliant in a darkened room, though definitely not as soft and fuzzy.  See the 2nd place entry by bod for a <i>fantastic</i> of what these plasma balls look like in real time.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-22 11:22:02.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Dave Gordon:Are the colors this brilliant to the naked eye, or do they depend on a photgraphic medium to bring them out? They are this brilliant in a darkened room, though definitely not as soft and fuzzy.  See the 2nd place entry by bod for a fantastic of what these plasma balls look like in real time.', '2003-10-22 12:21:41.000000', '2003-10-22 12:22:02.000000', 0),
(458205, 41831, 9149, '<td valign="top">I think this is an extremly nice photo. Nice color, nice contrast, nice focus. And I think this photo could illustrate the Newton''s First Law (''Every object in a state of uniform motion tends to remain in that state of motion unless an external force is applied to it'') because this photo shows equilibrium, that is a state of motion. And the boy is trying to compensate the external forces to maintain its state of motion. So, there is a strong relationship betweem this shot and challenge''s topic. Stronger than winner shot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-22 11:47:32.</i></td>', 'I think this is an extremly nice photo. Nice color, nice contrast, nice focus. And I think this photo could illustrate the Newton''s First Law (''Every object in a state of uniform motion tends to remain in that state of motion unless an external force is applied to it'') because this photo shows equilibrium, that is a state of motion. And the boy is trying to compensate the external forces to maintain its state of motion. So, there is a strong relationship betweem this shot and challenge''s topic. Stronger than winner shot.', '2003-10-22 12:47:07.000000', '2003-10-22 12:47:32.000000', 0),
