(458777, 42227, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pinback:</b></div><hr/><i>But where do you get your ideas - have you made a pact with the devil? :-)</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I really don''t have that much originality sometimes, if I don''t have my own ideas I just get inspired by what I have seen elsewhere. I think most people here in DPC do the same.</td>', 'Originally posted by pinback:But where do you get your ideas - have you made a pact with the devil? :-)  I really don''t have that much originality sometimes, if I don''t have my own ideas I just get inspired by what I have seen elsewhere. I think most people here in DPC do the same.', '2003-10-22 17:26:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(458844, 41917, 6870, '<td valign="top">Very nice, Matt, but not your best! I like many of your photos. This is stunning, though! My favorites include: Two Step, Tennis Balls, the photo with the concrete steps and the tree, and even the Matrix one. This is certainly up there! I suppose you had a hard time convincing people that this was ''scientific.'' I loved it during the challenge, and like it now, too!</td>', 'Very nice, Matt, but not your best! I like many of your photos. This is stunning, though! My favorites include: Two Step, Tennis Balls, the photo with the concrete steps and the tree, and even the Matrix one. This is certainly up there! I suppose you had a hard time convincing people that this was ''scientific.'' I loved it during the challenge, and like it now, too!', '2003-10-22 17:48:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(458855, 42109, 6870, '<td valign="top">My mistake, I asked my physicist father-in-law how many volts this was and he said, ''One inch? That''s about 60,000 volts.'' So my title is correct; the description is not. I corrected the title without correcting the description. Thanks for your votes; I''m surprised it did so well. There were many shots in this challenge I thought would whollup this one. Including YOURS probably!</td>', 'My mistake, I asked my physicist father-in-law how many volts this was and he said, ''One inch? That''s about 60,000 volts.'' So my title is correct; the description is not. I corrected the title without correcting the description. Thanks for your votes; I''m surprised it did so well. There were many shots in this challenge I thought would whollup this one. Including YOURS probably!', '2003-10-22 17:51:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(458881, 42104, 11677, '<td valign="top">I know this could have been better, but I really didn''t have much time during work to come up with something better.  Thanks for the comments.</td>', 'I know this could have been better, but I really didn''t have much time during work to come up with something better.  Thanks for the comments.', '2003-10-22 18:11:20.000000', NULL, 0),
