(459742, 42259, 9292, '<td valign="top">First of all, sorry for the spelling of Archimedes, I´m spanish. <br/>The duck was filled with water to achieve this splash. The slight <br/>discoloration at the top was due to incorrect fixation of the paper <br/>background. There was an unwanted  reflection of the sink over the duck´s<br/>face. I´ve discovered after the submission. After the submission I was in <br/>disagreement with the background, as one of you have pointed.<br/>Thanks for your comments.</td>', 'First of all, sorry for the spelling of Archimedes, I´m spanish. The duck was filled with water to achieve this splash. The slight discoloration at the top was due to incorrect fixation of the paper background. There was an unwanted  reflection of the sink over the duck´sface. I´ve discovered after the submission. After the submission I was in disagreement with the background, as one of you have pointed.Thanks for your comments.', '2003-10-23 07:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(459932, 42227, 13467, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwiness:</b></div><hr/><i>I used photoshop to crop and adjust the brightness/contrast and finally to sharpen and save for the web. Or how should I understand your comment?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Emm.... sorry... I think I don''t believe it. What the very very identical "marks" on the drops? <a href="//www.bystro.host.sk/drops.png" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.bystro.host.sk/drops.png</a> <br/> <br/>It looks like Copy &amp; Paste &amp; Resized drops. But maybe I''m wrong... so if it''s true sorry man, good shot. It''s a water?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-10-23 10:41:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kiwiness:I used photoshop to crop and adjust the brightness/contrast and finally to sharpen and save for the web. Or how should I understand your comment?  Emm.... sorry... I think I don''t believe it. What the very very identical "marks" on the drops? //www.bystro.host.sk/drops.png  It looks like Copy & Paste & Resized drops. But maybe I''m wrong... so if it''s true sorry man, good shot. It''s a water?', '2003-10-23 11:35:42.000000', '2003-10-23 11:41:15.000000', 0),
(459965, 41756, 10858, '<td valign="top">Too pixellated for me. Why don''t you use NeatImage or PhotoShop for noise reduction?</td>', 'Too pixellated for me. Why don''t you use NeatImage or PhotoShop for noise reduction?', '2003-10-23 12:07:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(460025, 42227, 5728, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bystro:</b></div><hr/><i>Emm.... sorry... I think I don''t believe it. What the very very identical "marks" on the drops? <br/>It looks like Copy &amp; Paste &amp; Resized drops. But maybe I''m wrong... so if it''s true sorry man, good shot. It''s a water?</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You are entitled to your opinion that''s fine with me. In a way it is a compliment knowing I can get people to think I had to manipulate the photo to achieve this effect.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.pbase.com/image/22581979" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Here</a> is one of the outakes I have that shows you that it is in fact very unmanipulated.</td>', 'Originally posted by Bystro:Emm.... sorry... I think I don''t believe it. What the very very identical "marks" on the drops? It looks like Copy & Paste & Resized drops. But maybe I''m wrong... so if it''s true sorry man, good shot. It''s a water?  You are entitled to your opinion that''s fine with me. In a way it is a compliment knowing I can get people to think I had to manipulate the photo to achieve this effect. Here is one of the outakes I have that shows you that it is in fact very unmanipulated.', '2003-10-23 12:44:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(460052, 42227, 656, '<td valign="top">The identical marks come from the soft box used.<br/> <br/> <br/>You can see similar reflections in the eyes of any model shot under studio lights - its pretty common...</td>', 'The identical marks come from the soft box used.  You can see similar reflections in the eyes of any model shot under studio lights - its pretty common...', '2003-10-23 13:13:55.000000', NULL, 0),
