(466049, 42227, 7275, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!!!!!<br/> <br/>Hi Gary,<br/>Coming back after 6 months break, I was not surprised to see your name under this Pic''. I showed your last works and I must say that you have ideas and a very very good technic. Since you got your Canon Cam, you<br/>H''v got fly :) :) :)<br/>Weiter Gary du bist gut!<br/></td>', 'Congratulations!!!!! Hi Gary,Coming back after 6 months break, I was not surprised to see your name under this Pic''. I showed your last works and I must say that you have ideas and a very very good technic. Since you got your Canon Cam, youH''v got fly :) :) :)Weiter Gary du bist gut!', '2003-10-29 13:44:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(474979, 42221, 9889, '<td valign="top">A note of which I am pride:<br/>this photo was not cropped, I intended to compose it as it is.<br/> <br/>And a trick shared: I shot this photo at 1/3 of sec without tripod! =)<br/>Impossible? Yes and no. <br/> <br/>There was a very clean glass in front of the subject and I pressed the camera lens against it completely and firmly.<br/> <br/>That created a position which, possibly, was even more stable than the one I would have achieved with a tripod, and in conjunction with the swiveling body of the f707 (a too underrated and very important feature of a camera IMHO) it helped the pcik the composition and made crop unnecessary.<br/> <br/>Roger: ''a bit of a nothing..."? Considering how interestingly contrasting is your sentence, I take it as a complement.<br/></td>', 'A note of which I am pride:this photo was not cropped, I intended to compose it as it is. And a trick shared: I shot this photo at 1/3 of sec without tripod! =)Impossible? Yes and no.  There was a very clean glass in front of the subject and I pressed the camera lens against it completely and firmly. That created a position which, possibly, was even more stable than the one I would have achieved with a tripod, and in conjunction with the swiveling body of the f707 (a too underrated and very important feature of a camera IMHO) it helped the pcik the composition and made crop unnecessary. Roger: ''a bit of a nothing..."? Considering how interestingly contrasting is your sentence, I take it as a complement.', '2003-11-06 02:31:52.000000', NULL, 0),
