(909504, 42130, 22748, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bod, the master himself:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Print version has been cleaned up using Fred Miranda''s ISOX Pro noise reduction plugin (not DPC legal?).<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>NeatImage is definitely DPC legal and I don''t see why ISOX wouldn''t be also. As long as it''s applied to the whole image and there is no selective editing going on I believe it would be legal.</td>', 'Originally posted by bod, the master himself: Print version has been cleaned up using Fred Miranda''s ISOX Pro noise reduction plugin (not DPC legal?).  NeatImage is definitely DPC legal and I don''t see why ISOX wouldn''t be also. As long as it''s applied to the whole image and there is no selective editing going on I believe it would be legal.', '2004-09-14 15:27:14.000000', NULL, 0),
